  "answer": "The Aral Sea shrunk primarily due to the diversion of the Syr Darya River for irrigation, which reduced freshwater flow into the sea. This led to the shrinking of the sea and the eventual drying up of the region. The process was exacerbated by climate change and human activities, resulting in the formation of the Aralkum Desert and the loss of the once-prosperous fishing industry."
